// An imported file's names used to be spliced into the caller's scope with no
// prefix and no way to rename, so two files could not both define `size`.
//
// `as` namespaces them. A module IS a namespace, so this needs no machinery the
// language does not already have — and an alias is checked like any other
// module, members included.
import "_geometry" as Geo
println(Geo.size)
println(Geo.area(3, 4))

// The names do not join this scope, so Enum.size is still Enum.size.
println(Enum.size([1, 2, 3]))
